## Context

Fourth tranche (tracker 0550): the compute stages. The micro-batch
becomes the schedulable unit everywhere, sized by the ratified quantum.

## Relevant files

- SPEC.md §5.2.5 (quantum ~1 s ratified, EWMA autotune with per-step
  clamp [0,5, 2], fixed-cost floor, memory ceiling; claim TTL 30 × the
  quantum; sidecar ordering: append, fsync, then commit the row),
  DECISIONS.md 2026-09-01 (quantum ruling, slow/stuck split),
  bench/results/0481-gpu-anomaly (flat-throughput finding the autotune
  wording rests on).

## Actions

1. Chunk worker over stored text, keyed idempotent derivations.
2. Embed worker: batch packed to a token budget, length-sorted; size
   autotuned to the quantum (EWMA, step clamp, floor, ceiling); yields
   between micro-batches (activity file, holder check, queue re-read).
3. Claim TTL = 30 × quantum; expired claims reclaimable; duplicate
   compute bounded to one micro-batch — test it, don't assert it.
4. Sidecar writes per SPEC's ordering; generation stamping.

## Test

- Red first: on the injected clock with a stubbed engine of programmable
  per-item cost, the autotuned size converges to the quantum for two
  synthetic devices (fast/slow) and oscillation stays inside the step
  clamp when the cost curve is made non-monotonic.

## Verification

- [ ] A worker killed mid-batch: claim expires at 30 × quantum, another
      finishes it, exactly one commit (CAS guard)
- [ ] Incumbent MiniLM vectors byte-identical to stock upstream's

## Invariants

- Vector fingerprint handshake per SPEC §5.2.5; upstream tests green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Both stages merged on a fork branch, convergence + TTL tests green
